  "result": "`slugify` is implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes: 12 tests, none failing.\n\nIt follows your rules:\n- **Diacritics:** `đ` and `Đ` become `d`, and other accents are stripped, so Vietnamese and other Latin text comes out as plain ASCII.\n- **Separators:** each run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen, and leading and trailing hyphens are removed.\n- **Length:** the slug is cut to 50 characters, then any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed.\n\nI added 10 tests for it to `test/strings.test.js`, next to the existing `capitalize` ones. They cover:\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- runs of symbols\n- trimming of leading and trailing hyphens\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- digits\n- the 50-character cut, both when it lands on a hyphen and when it doesn't\n\nThe function converts its input with `String(text)`, so `null` gives `\"null\"` and `undefined` gives `\"undefined\"`. Your rules didn't say what to do there, so tell me if you'd rather those return an empty string.",
